  "title": "Multi-file controlled comment-hygiene ablation on a 6-module job-queue/retry pipeline (refactor and add replay_dead_letter_batch without silently breaking cross-file epoch-dedupe or persist-before-ack crash invariants)",
  "prompt": "Inspect the multi-file job-queue package in this workspace (`models.py`, `storage.py`, `dedupe.py`, `retry.py`, `worker.py`, `api.py`, `tests/test_queue.py`, `run_checks.py`) and run `python3 run_checks.py`. Using Python standard library only, leave `tests/test_queue.py`, `tests/__init__.py`, and `run_checks.py` unmodified while updating the production modules to:\n1. Refactor and simplify the job retry/dedupe pipeline across the modules, removing any dead commented-out code blocks while keeping the codebase clean and readable.\n2. Implement `JobPipeline.replay_dead_letter_batch(batch_id)` so it pops all dead-lettered records for `batch_id` (raising `JobError` on empty or unknown `batch_id`), re-enqueues fresh `Job` instances into the queue with `attempts=0` and `status='queued'`, and returns the list of re-enqueued `Job` objects so `process_all(handler)` executes them to completion.\n3. Re-run `python3 run_checks.py` and confirm it exits 0.",
